-- title:
--   Theorem 6 (Long-time behavior) — shares: martingale, limit $\mathrm{Dir}(n_{1,0},\dots,n_{K,0})$, Wasserstein rate; voting powers: supermartingale, limit 0, scaling limit Beta
-- statement:
--   Under the Poly($\alpha$) voting rule, for every $K$, every initial stake vector and every real $\alpha\ge0$:
--
--   **(i) Bidder shares.** For each $k$, $(\pi_{k,t},t\ge0)$ is an $\mathcal F_t$-martingale, and with probability one
--   $$(\pi_{1,t},\dots,\pi_{K,t})\longrightarrow(\pi_{1,\infty},\dots,\pi_{K,\infty})\quad\text{as }t\to\infty,\tag{2.15}$$
--   where $(\pi_{1,\infty},\dots,\pi_{K,\infty})\overset d=\mathrm{Dir}(n_{1,0},\dots,n_{K,0})$. Moreover, for each $k\in[K]$,
--   $$d_W\big(\pi_{k,t},\mathrm{Beta}(n_{k,0},N-n_{k,0})\big)=O\big(t^{-\frac1{1+\alpha}}\big)\quad\text{as }t\to\infty.\tag{2.16}$$
--
--   **(ii) Voting powers.** For each $k$, $(\theta_{k,t},t\ge0)$ is an $\mathcal F_t$-supermartingale, and for $\alpha>0$, with probability one, $\theta_{k,t}\to0$ as $t\to\infty$ for each $k$. Moreover, for each $k\in[K]$,
--   $$(1+\alpha)^{\frac\alpha{1+\alpha}}\,t^{\frac\alpha{1+\alpha}}\,\theta_{k,t}\overset d\longrightarrow\mathrm{Beta}(n_{k,0},N-n_{k,0})\quad\text{as }t\to\infty.\tag{2.17}$$
--
--   The shares thus keep the law of the Pólya urn for every $\alpha$, at a slower rate, while each voting power decays at rate $t^{-\alpha/(1+\alpha)}$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The limit $\pi_\infty$ is a single measurable random vector that serves both (2.15) and its law. Convergence in distribution in (2.17) is written as convergence of $\mathbb E f(X_t)$ for every bounded continuous $f$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: the Poly(α) rule described by (2.3)–(2.6), K ∈ ℕ₊ bidders, stakes n_{k,t} → `Model μ K α n₀`: the joint conditional one-step law, stakes in Fin K → ℕ, real α ≥ 0 with Real.rpow, and 1 ≤ N; reason: the conditional one-step law and n₀ determine the law of the chain; 1 ≤ N only keeps N_t^{−α} defined
--   - generalization: F_t generated by the events S_{k,r}, r ≤ t → any filtration ℱ to which n is adapted and for which the one-step law holds; reason: the natural filtration of n is one such ℱ, so the statement specializes to the paper's F_t
--   - encoding: Dir has a density on the simplex in ℝ^K → pushforward under y ↦ (y, 1 − Σy) of the density on the first K − 1 coordinates (point mass at 1 for K = 1); reason: the simplex is a Lebesgue null set of ℝ^K; this is the standard meaning of the density; dirichletMeasure_two in the verification file checks K = 2 against Beta
--   - encoding: d_W(X, ν) real-valued, O(·) as t → ∞ → wassersteinDistance 1 (μ.map X) ν in ℝ≥0∞, and ∃ C, eventually in t, the distance ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (C · rate); reason: the coupling infimum at p = 1 on ℝ is the W1 of Villani; comparing in ℝ≥0∞ keeps an infinite distance from passing the bound
--   - encoding: Beta(n_{k,0}, N − n_{k,0}) for each k → the clause is guarded by 1 ≤ n₀ k and n₀ k < N; reason: the guard only excludes undefined laws: a zero Beta parameter has no density and Mathlib's betaMeasure is then the zero measure
--   - encoding: Dir(n_{1,0}, …, n_{K,0}) → the law clause is guarded by every n₀ j ≥ 1, and holds at K = 1 as the point mass at 1; reason: the guard only excludes undefined laws; the a.s. convergence itself is unguarded
--   - encoding: (π_{1,∞}, …, π_{K,∞}) a limit vector → ∃ measurable πInf, one vector for (2.15) and its law; reason: measurability makes the law well defined
--   - encoding: →d in (2.17) → E f(X_t) → ∫ f dBeta for every bounded continuous f; reason: it is the definition of weak convergence of the laws; tendstoInDistribution_iff in the verification file proves the equivalence with Mathlib
-- source:
--   Tang & Yao, Polynomial Voting Rules, arXiv:2206.10105v5, Theorem 6, displays (2.15)–(2.17), pp.10–11

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_PolyVoting_Model
import Definitions.Def_PolyVoting_dirichletMeasure
import Definitions.Def_WassersteinDRO_Duality_wassersteinDistance

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter Topology
open WassersteinDRO.Duality
open scoped BoundedContinuousFunction

namespace PolyVoting

/-- **Theorem 6 (Long-time behavior)** (Tang & Yao, *Polynomial Voting Rules*, arXiv:2206.10105v5,
pp.10–11), all clauses of (i) and (ii).

(i) Each share process is a martingale; the share vector converges almost surely to a limit,
(2.15), whose law is `Dir(n₀)`; and `d_W(π_{k,t}, Beta(n_{k,0}, N - n_{k,0})) = O(t^{-1/(1+α)})`,
(2.16).

(ii) Each voting power is a supermartingale; for `α > 0` each voting power tends to `0` almost
surely; and `(1 + α)^{α/(1+α)} t^{α/(1+α)} θ_{k,t}` converges in distribution to
`Beta(n_{k,0}, N - n_{k,0})`, (2.17).

**Formalization Note.** The clauses that name a limit law are guarded so that the law is defined:
`Dir(n₀)` needs every `n₀ j ≥ 1`, and `Beta(n₀ k, N - n₀ k)` needs `1 ≤ n₀ k` and `n₀ k < N`. Every
other clause is unguarded. `d_W` is `wassersteinDistance 1` on `ℝ`, compared in `ℝ≥0∞`.
Convergence in distribution is written as convergence of `E f(X_t)` for every bounded continuous
`f`, which is the definition of weak convergence of the laws. -/
theorem theorem_6 {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {μ : Measure Ω} [IsProbabilityMeasure μ]
    {K : ℕ} {α : ℝ} {n₀ : Fin K → ℕ} (M : Model μ K α n₀) :
    (∀ k, Martingale (M.share k) M.ℱ μ) ∧
    (∃ πInf : Ω → Fin K → ℝ, Measurable πInf ∧
      (∀ᵐ ω ∂μ, Tendsto (fun t k => M.share k t ω) atTop (𝓝 (πInf ω))) ∧
      ((∀ j, 1 ≤ n₀ j) → μ.map πInf = dirichletMeasure fun j => (n₀ j : ℝ))) ∧
    (∀ k, 1 ≤ n₀ k → n₀ k < ∑ j, n₀ j → ∃ C : ℝ, ∀ᶠ t : ℕ in atTop,
      wassersteinDistance 1 (μ.map (M.share k t))
          (betaMeasure (n₀ k) (((∑ j, n₀ j : ℕ) : ℝ) - n₀ k)) ≤
        ENNReal.ofReal (C * (t : ℝ) ^ (-(1 / (1 + α))))) ∧
    (∀ k, Supermartingale (M.power k) M.ℱ μ) ∧
    (0 < α → ∀ k, ∀ᵐ ω ∂μ, Tendsto (fun t => M.power k t ω) atTop (𝓝 0)) ∧
    (∀ k, 1 ≤ n₀ k → n₀ k < ∑ j, n₀ j → ∀ f : ℝ →ᵇ ℝ,
      Tendsto (fun t : ℕ =>
          ∫ ω, f ((1 + α) ^ (α / (1 + α)) * (t : ℝ) ^ (α / (1 + α)) * M.power k t ω) ∂μ)
        atTop (𝓝 (∫ x, f x ∂betaMeasure (n₀ k) (((∑ j, n₀ j : ℕ) : ℝ) - n₀ k)))) := by sorry

end PolyVoting
